  "prefLabel": "Pdab 101.03 Generic drug",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pdab 101.03 \"Generic drug\" means a prescription drug, whether identified by its chemical, proprietary, or nonproprietary name, that is not a brand-name drug and is therapeutically equivalent to a brand-name drug in dosage, safety, strength, method of consumption, quality, performance, and intended use. The term \"generic drug\" includes a biosimilar product as defined by 42 U.S.C. § 262(i)(2).\n\nSource. #13500-A, eff 12-2-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pdab100-300.html"
